<article class="env-lemma" id="07SH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07SH">Lemma <span data-tag="07SH">70.4.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $(X_ i, f_{ii'})$ be an inverse system over $I$ of algebraic spaces over $S$ with affine transition maps. Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _ i X_ i$. Let $0 \in I$. Suppose that $T \to X_0$ is a morphism of algebraic spaces. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{X_0} X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{i \geq 0} T \times _{X_0} X_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> as algebraic spaces over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The limit $X$ is an algebraic space by Lemma <a href="/tag/07SF" data-tag="07SF">70.4.1</a>. The equality is formal, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/002M" data-tag="002M">4.14.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>